1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:10,026
So expanding from A to the same final volume, the adiabatic path ends at a lower pressure, encloses less area, and does less work.

2
00:00:10,026 --> 00:00:19,023
With no heat coming in, it pays for every joule out of its own internal energy, and that is why an adiabatic expansion cools the gas.

